{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED and validated live. Change 1702 submitted, merged as 04b78f5e7e (Gerrit rebased it server-side from my local 6faf9c3440). Worktree realigned to the merged commit via the gerrit remote.\n\nLIVE VALIDATION — this ticket's own close, on the merged code:\n\n    23:49:13  COMPLETION_VERDICT cfcb   <- LLM verifier finished (runs outside the lock)\n    23:49:24  STATUS cfcb               <- the close write\n    23:49:27  SIGNATURE cfcb            <- attestation\n    (no COMPACT commit — none exists for this ticket, ever)\n\nThe entire post-verify tail took 14 seconds, and there is no compaction lock hold at all. Compare the incident that opened this investigation, same tail on the old code:\n\n    20:35:47  STATUS 271c\n    20:35:49  SIGNATURE 271c\n    20:35:52  .ticket-write.lock.d created\n    20:49:45  COMPACT 271c              <- 13m53s of continuous store-lock hold\n\nOne caveat on how to read this, so the number is not overclaimed: the close's WALL CLOCK was 349s, and that is NOT lock hold and never was. It is the LLM completion verifier, which has always run outside the write lock (proven earlier in this investigation, and the reason the original premise of sunlit-cynical-ray was falsified). The metric that moved is the lock-held tail after the verdict: from up to 13m53s down to the three short per-append acquisitions visible above.\n\nClosed with --class=preexisting: the defect long predates this session — compaction has been inline on close since the close gate was built, and bug 7084 measured the same holder at 48.1s before store growth pushed it into minutes.\n\nClosing this unblocked gaudy-gangrenous-basilisk (1fde-becd-942a-4351), story B, which restores an automatic compaction trigger out of band. Moving to it now: with the depends_on prerequisite closed, review-plan will actually run instead of fast-failing.\n\nAlso filed from the CI triage: unheedful-custodial-bluebottle (f7da-baae-3c93-47e2), linked discovered_from — the shared git seam does not retry write-side temp-file faults, so one known-transient fault class self-heals in event_append's git add and is fatal for every other store git caller."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786603809133810001,"uuid":"a14f010e-0e0b-4fde-b673-d81121e57597"}